I was once asked this in an interview.  I didn't manage to answer it live in
the time allotted, but I liked the problem, took it home and finished the
solution on my own.

Given:
* An equivalence relational operator = (e.g., X = 0, Y = A etc.);
* A loop operator LOOP (e.g., for/while loop);
* An addition operator (e.g., X = X + 1).

Produce:
* Given variables X and Y, produce an algorithm to generate Y = X - 1.
  There are *no* conditional (if/then) or substraction operators available.
